1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,068
Welcome to Lesson 4.4, Documenting the Monthly Clinical Review.

2
00:00:06,333 --> 00:00:11,122
This is Part 1 of 2: Allergies, Medications, and Numbers to Track.

3
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,237
Each month, you review the patient's records,

4
00:00:15,287 --> 00:00:19,589
and post updates in the Clinical Review sub-tab of Care Management.

5
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:22,596
Those updates appear in the patient report.

6
00:00:22,867 --> 00:00:25,883
In this part, you'll post the first three sections.

7
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:31,666
Allergies: an allergy review, or a note that the patient has no known allergies.

8
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:37,024
Medications: a note that the medication list was reviewed and updated.

9
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:41,242
And Numbers to Track: the most recent labs, the latest vitals,

10
00:00:41,292 --> 00:00:44,382
and any lab that's missing or not recent.

11
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:50,260
This lesson continues with the scratch patient from the earlier lessons.

12
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:54,235
You've created the profile, completed the initial assessment,

13
00:00:54,285 --> 00:00:56,333
and updated Clinical Data.

14
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,560
Now you'll document this month's clinical review.

15
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:13,597
Open the Care Management tab.

16
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:17,501
At the top, the Task Type is Monthly Clinical Review.

17
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:20,504
It's performed by you, and dated today.

18
00:01:21,367 --> 00:01:23,955
Scroll down to the workflow sub-tabs.

19
00:01:24,233 --> 00:01:28,937
On the way, you pass the patient's conditions, care team, and time logs.

20
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:36,332
The monthly review uses two of them: Clinical Review, and Problems.

21
00:01:41,967 --> 00:01:43,927
Start with Clinical Review.

22
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:48,525
The updates you post here go into the patient report.

23
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:51,395
At the end of the review, you print that report,

24
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:54,376
and upload it to Practice Fusion for billing.

25
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:57,924
Scroll down to the review sections.

26
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:01,902
On the left, each section shows what you entered in Clinical Data,

27
00:02:01,952 --> 00:02:03,880
so it's already filled in.

28
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:06,719
On the right, each section has a notes column.

29
00:02:06,769 --> 00:02:09,625
That's where you post this month's update.

30
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:13,119
Start with Allergies, near the bottom of the page.

31
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:21,157
If the patient has allergies, you've already added them in Clinical Data.

32
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:24,391
Click Allergies, at the top of Allergy Notes.

33
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:27,786
The Allergies window lists the patient's allergies.

34
00:02:27,836 --> 00:02:30,710
This patient is allergic to penicillin.

35
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:33,594
To post an update, first select the allergies.

36
00:02:33,644 --> 00:02:36,655
The checkbox in the header selects them all.

37
00:02:36,933 --> 00:02:41,879
A template list appears: Select update regarding selected allergies.

38
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:46,616
Open it, and choose Allergies Reviewed with patient, no Changes.

39
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,683
Then click Post Update.

40
00:02:50,933 --> 00:02:56,067
The update is posted in Allergy Notes, with today's date and the allergy list.

41
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:01,875
If the patient has no known allergies, don't use the Allergies button.

42
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,742
Click Add Update instead.

43
00:03:05,792 --> 00:03:07,834
It adds a free-text note.

44
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:13,029
For no known allergies, always use this fixed text, exactly as written:

45
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,510
No known allergies have been added.

46
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:21,207
Due to system limitations, we can only add this update as a note.

47
00:03:21,467 --> 00:03:23,887
Paste it in the note, and click Save.

48
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:28,396
This patient does have an allergy, so here the note is only an example,

49
00:03:28,446 --> 00:03:31,126
and the window is closed with Cancel.

50
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:36,370
So there are two cases.

51
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:40,795
If the patient has allergies, select them in the Allergies window,

52
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:45,953
and post a template, such as Allergies Reviewed with patient, no Changes.

53
00:03:48,933 --> 00:03:53,115
If there are none, use Add Update with the no-known-allergies note.

54
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:55,959
Next, Medications.

55
00:03:59,167 --> 00:04:02,626
Click Medications, at the top of Medication Notes.

56
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:08,327
This opens the medication list you reviewed and reconciled in Clinical Data.

57
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:12,332
Below the list, you can see when it was last reconciled.

58
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:16,199
Select all the medications with the header checkbox.

59
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:22,314
Open the template list, and choose Medication list reviewed and updated.

60
00:04:22,567 --> 00:04:24,450
Then click Post Update.

61
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:27,534
The note is posted in Medication Notes.

62
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,424
Next is Numbers to Track.

63
00:04:30,474 --> 00:04:33,692
It covers two things: labs, and vitals.

64
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,128
Start with labs.

65
00:04:36,178 --> 00:04:39,623
Click Labs, at the top of Numbers to Track Notes.

66
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:44,106
The Lab Results window lists the results you added in Clinical Data,

67
00:04:44,156 --> 00:04:46,046
with their LOINC codes.

68
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:50,654
Select all of them with the header checkbox.

69
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:55,074
From the template list, choose Custom Update.

70
00:04:55,333 --> 00:04:59,101
In the custom update box, type: Most recent labs.

71
00:05:02,133 --> 00:05:04,016
Then click Post Update.

72
00:05:04,267 --> 00:05:09,579
The labs are posted under Most recent labs, each with its LOINC code and value.

73
00:05:10,433 --> 00:05:13,819
Vitals aren't lab results, so they're not in the Labs list.

74
00:05:13,869 --> 00:05:15,833
You add them as free text.

75
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:22,232
Click Add Update.

76
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:27,548
Add the basic vitals monitored for every patient: blood pressure, and weight.

77
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:32,759
If one of the patient's conditions needs another vital, add it too.

78
00:05:32,809 --> 00:05:38,791
For example, oxygen saturation for COPD, or pulse for atrial fibrillation.

79
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:43,822
Take the readings from the PointClickCare resident dashboard.

80
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:47,101
Copy the latest blood pressure, with its date,

81
00:05:47,367 --> 00:05:49,667
and the latest weight, with its date.

82
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:58,145
Back in ThoroughCare, paste them into the note.

83
00:05:59,667 --> 00:06:04,352
Before you finish the note, check which labs the patient's conditions require.

84
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:11,649
Open the Update Care Policy sheet, on the Numbers To Track tab.

85
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:15,620
For each CCM condition, it lists the numbers to track,

86
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:20,727
with their LOINC codes, normal levels, and recency period in days.

87
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,580
This patient's CCM condition is hypertension.

88
00:06:24,833 --> 00:06:30,805
For hypertension, that's blood pressure, hemoglobin and hematocrit, BUN,

89
00:06:30,855 --> 00:06:34,234
creatinine and GFR, the cholesterol panel

90
00:06:34,284 --> 00:06:38,330
and triglycerides, hemoglobin A1C, and TSH.

91
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:41,608
Compare that list with the patient's results.

92
00:06:41,658 --> 00:06:43,535
Here, there's no TSH.

93
00:06:44,867 --> 00:06:47,297
Also check how old each result is.

94
00:06:47,347 --> 00:06:50,642
Each lab has a recency period, in days.

95
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:54,742
Kidney function, for example, is 180 days.

96
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,785
If the latest result is older than that, it isn't recent.

97
00:06:59,067 --> 00:07:01,476
Missing labs, and labs that aren't recent,

98
00:07:01,526 --> 00:07:04,551
must be noted, so they're monitored on time.

99
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:08,050
Other conditions, such as hyperlipidemia, COPD,

100
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:12,304
or depression, have their own lists in the same sheet.

101
00:07:15,133 --> 00:07:19,322
Back in ThoroughCare, the most recent labs are already posted.

102
00:07:20,833 --> 00:07:23,809
Click Add Update again, and paste the vitals.

103
00:07:26,133 --> 00:07:31,420
Under the vitals, add a line for each lab that's missing or not recent.

104
00:07:31,470 --> 00:07:33,874
Here, type: no recent TSH.

105
00:07:34,433 --> 00:07:35,963
Then click Save.

106
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,247
The note is saved: the vitals, the missing lab,

107
00:07:39,297 --> 00:07:41,842
and the most recent labs below it.

108
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:46,192
That completes Allergies, Medications, and Numbers to Track.

109
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,759
To recap.

110
00:07:50,033 --> 00:07:53,640
Open the Clinical Review sub-tab in Care Management.

111
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,993
For allergies, select them all and post a template,

112
00:07:57,043 --> 00:07:59,650
or add the no-known-allergies note.

113
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:04,129
For medications, post Medication list reviewed and updated.

114
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:08,129
For labs, post a custom update: Most recent labs.

115
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:11,544
Add the latest blood pressure and weight as free text,

116
00:08:11,594 --> 00:08:13,996
plus any vital a condition needs.

117
00:08:14,267 --> 00:08:18,565
Check the care policy, note any missing or old labs, and save.

118
00:08:21,033 --> 00:08:22,940
That's the end of Part 1.

119
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,720
Next, in Part 2: Resources and Support,

120
00:08:25,770 --> 00:08:28,921
and Other Provider and Appointment Notes.
